hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1203","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Sa’id bin Abi Hind told us, Sallam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us On the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Salim Abi Al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The best prayer for a person is in his home except the obligatory prayer.” Pindar said: “The best of your prayers is in your homes, except for the obligatory prayers.”"
"1204","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Qaisi told us, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Musa bin Uqba told us, he said: I heard Salim Abul Nadr speaking, On the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray, O people, in your homes, for the best A person’s prayer is in his home, except for the obligatory prayers.”"
